# Work tracking (GitHub)

This repo uses **GitHub** ([Unthred/BuildMonitor](https://github.com/Unthred/BuildMonitor)) — **Issues**, **Projects**, and `gh` CLI, not Azure DevOps.

**Primary view:** the [BuildMonitor project board (#3)](https://github.com/users/Unthred/projects/3). Issues exist to back cards on that board; an issue not on the board is untracked work.

## Conventions

- **Default assignee:** **@me** (Simon) for every new issue unless the user names someone else.
- **Project board (mandatory):** [BuildMonitor (#3)](https://github.com/users/Unthred/projects/3) — **every issue is added to the project** at creation (`gh project item-add 3 …`). Config: [.github/project.json](../../.github/project.json). CLI: [docs/ops/github-workflow.md](../../docs/ops/github-workflow.md).
- **Features and enhancements:** GitHub **Issue** with a clear title.
- **Defects:** Issue with prefix `Bug:` when helpful.
- **Branches:** `feature/<id>-short-kebab-name` (example: `feature/42-live-build-log`). No direct feature commits on `main`.
- **Pull requests:** every change lands via PR; body must include `Closes #<id>` (see [.github/pull_request_template.md](../../.github/pull_request_template.md)).
- **Commits:** prefix with `#<id>:` when an issue applies (example: `#42: Debounce run log saves`).

## Every change (mandatory)

**No untracked work.** Every code, docs, rules, or behaviour change needs an issue, a feature branch, and a merged PR — unless the user explicitly opts out (see **Exception** below).

| Step | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Start | Issue exists **and is on project #3** (Status **Todo** or **In Progress**) |
| Work | Branch `feature/<id>-...`; commit with `#<id>:` prefix |
| Review | PR with `Closes #<id>`; board Status **In Progress** |
| Done | PR **squash-merged** to `main`; issue **closed**; board Status **Done** |

Before `git commit`, `git push`, **ship it**, or **check in** when the user did not give an issue number:

1. **Use a supplied id** — `#42`, “for issue 42”, or branch `feature/42-...`.
2. **Resolve one** (in order):
   - Current branch name `feature/<id>-...`
   - Conversation + files changed (feature area, doc title)
   - **Project board #3** — **Todo** / **In Progress** cards matching keywords (preferred over bare issue list)
   - `gh issue list` on the repo (if found, confirm it is on project #3; if not, add it before commit)
3. **If exactly one plausible item** — tell the user which `#` you chose, then commit with that link.
4. **If several fit or none fit** — **ask** (list candidates with id + title) or offer to **create** a new issue (assigned @me), **`gh project item-add 3`**, then branch. Do not commit until `#` is agreed and the card is on the board.
5. **Do not** push work to `main` without an issue and PR unless the user explicitly asks for a direct-to-main hotfix.

**After linking:** set project Status to **In Progress** when starting substantial work; **Done** only when the user says ship/merge or work is complete on `main` (issue closed).

**Board backlog:** run `.\scripts\github\Sync-ProjectBoard.ps1` when retrospective or planned cards are missing; see [docs/ops/github-workflow.md](../../docs/ops/github-workflow.md).

**Hooks (mandatory locally):** run `.\scripts\install-githooks.ps1` once per clone — `commit-msg` rejects commits without `#<issue>` (or `feature/<id>-...` branch). PRs must reference an issue (CI workflow).

**Exception:** user explicitly says “no issue”, “chore only”, or “docs/rules only, skip issue”.

## Agent automation (`gh`)

**Always create issue + add to project in one flow** — never leave a repo issue off the board.

```powershell
# Issue + project #3 (both steps required)
$url = gh issue create --repo Unthred/BuildMonitor --title "..." --body "..." --assignee @me --json url -q .url
gh project item-add 3 --owner Unthred --url $url

# Existing issue missing from the board
gh project item-add 3 --owner Unthred --url "https://github.com/Unthred/BuildMonitor/issues/42"

gh issue view 42 --repo Unthred/BuildMonitor
gh issue list --repo Unthred/BuildMonitor --state open
gh pr create --title "#42: ..." --body "Closes #42`n`n..."
gh pr merge <n> --squash
```

Details, project setup, and Status field updates: [docs/ops/github-workflow.md](../../docs/ops/github-workflow.md).

## “Ship it” (agent)

When the user says **ship** or **ship it**, follow **`feature-ship`** skill:

1. Commit + push on `feature/<id>-...`
2. Create PR if none (`Closes #<id>` in body); issue / project **In Progress**
3. **Merge** the PR into `main` (when user asked for full ship)
4. Issue **closed**; project Status **Done**

**Ready for review** / **open PR** → commit + push + active PR only; do not merge unless asked.

## Record of intent

Chat and Cursor plan files are not the system of record. The **BuildMonitor project board (#3)**, backed by **GitHub Issues**, **PR descriptions**, and **`docs/`**, are.
